WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Wednesday,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.440
the fourth of November. This
episode is written with AI,

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.080
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.920
Middle East crude is now in surplus,
and the Dubai benchmark has slipped

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.120
into contango for the
first time since July.

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.360
Diesel is a different story:
the world is still short,

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.413
and that looks set to
last well into next year.

8
00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:27.280
Meanwhile Brent swung hard on conflicting
peace headlines after Washington

9
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.360
confirmed a strike on Iran's Qeshm Island.

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.840
On the markets. Brent was back
around one hundred and four dollars a

11
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.693
barrel on Tuesday after
a volatile morning.

12
00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:40.000
The spread between the front and
third-month Dubai contracts was near

13
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.720
zero this week. In Europe, gas storage
was seventy-four point three percent

14
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.000
full on the second of November, down
about a quarter of a point on the

15
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.920
day, according to Gas
Infrastructure Europe.

16
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.960
And in the US, the American Petroleum
Institute estimates a crude stock

17
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.640
draw of about five point three million
barrels in the week to the thirtieth

18
00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.800
of October.

19
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.840
Starting with the Gulf. The November
Dubai contract has moved into contango

20
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.040
for the first time since early
July, according to OilPrice dot com.

21
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.627
That's a sign Middle East crude
supply now exceeds demand.

22
00:01:11.653 --> 00:01:15.520
The reason is volume. Gulf producers
have stepped up shuttle shipping

23
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.440
through Hormuz, moving cargoes ship
to ship in the Gulf of Oman once

24
00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.160
tankers clear the strait.

25
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.480
Physical flows have been rising
gradually for two months.

26
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.587
This matters for Asian refiners.

27
00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:30.320
The Dubai cash-to-futures spread is
routinely used to set official selling

28
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.320
prices for Gulf grades, so a flatter
curve feeds straight into what Asian

29
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.560
buyers pay. That could mean softer
official prices for medium sour crude

30
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.120
loading in December.

31
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.320
Cheaper freight is also
reopening long-haul trades.

32
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.960
Bharat Petroleum bought one million
barrels of West Texas Intermediate

33
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.627
for delivery to Mumbai, Reuters reported.

34
00:01:49.653 --> 00:01:52.747
The cargo arrives between late
December and early January,

35
00:01:52.773 --> 00:01:56.120
priced at about eighteen dollars
a barrel over Dated Brent.

36
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.480
Freight has eased from the
records it hit in early October.

37
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.440
The crude surplus hasn't
reached refined products.

38
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.080
Asian crude imports are
back at pre-war levels,

39
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.013
according to OilPrice dot com.

40
00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.653
But imports of gasoline,
and especially diesel,

41
00:02:09.707 --> 00:02:12.800
from the Middle East have collapsed,
because refining capacity there

42
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.040
is reduced. OilPrice expects the
diesel crunch to run well into next

43
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:17.867
year.

44
00:02:17.893 --> 00:02:20.200
Globally, there's been a partial recovery.

45
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.320
Kpler data show refinery inputs fell
by four point eight million barrels

46
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.240
a day in the second quarter.

47
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.240
That was a six percent drop.

48
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.520
In the third quarter, throughput
recovered by one point eight million

49
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.120
barrels a day as refiners
adapted to new trade flows.

50
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.120
Fuel oil is tight too, which
shipowners will already have noticed.

51
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.880
Very low sulphur fuel oil bunkers in
Singapore topped a thousand dollars

52
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.840
a tonne in October,
according to Ship and Bunker.

53
00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.080
That's the first time since March.

54
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.840
In the US, distillate stocks stood at
about one hundred and three million

55
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.320
barrels in the week to the
twenty-third of October,

56
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.160
according to the EIA. That was down
about one and a half million barrels

57
00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.080
on the week.

58
00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.840
Now to Iran. US officials have
confirmed a strike on Qeshm Island,

59
00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.040
near Hormuz, on Monday, the
Wall Street Journal reported.

60
00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.960
They described it as one of a series of
limited strikes that hadn't previously

61
00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.840
been disclosed.

62
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.320
Brent was pulled in both directions.

63
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.440
It closed Monday at one hundred
and four dollars eighty,

64
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.520
after a seven point six percent fall.

65
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.160
It rebounded overnight
on the strike report.

66
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.560
Then on Tuesday morning, conflicting
reports on peace talks sent it from

67
00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.320
one hundred and seven dollars twenty
down to one hundred dollars eighty,

68
00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.440
before it recovered.

69
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.680
The diplomatic picture is murky.

70
00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.440
A diplomat briefed on the matter
told Rigzone both sides are reviewing

71
00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.360
new proposals from mediators.

72
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.360
Tehran, though, dismissed
the reports of momentum.

73
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.440
Neither government has confirmed the
terms or the status of any talks.

74
00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.480
Looking further ahead, Rystad Energy
sees a limited deal as possible

75
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.920
by the middle of next year.

76
00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.960
Even then, it says, Hormuz flows are
unlikely to return to pre-war levels.

77
00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.280
Turning to gas. Europe enters the
heating season with its lowest gas

78
00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:05.200
storage in over a decade, according
to the International Energy Agency.

79
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.480
The agency expects the global market
to stay tight well into next year.

80
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.240
American cargoes are
filling part of the gap.

81
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.560
US exports to Europe were about six
point nine million tonnes in October,

82
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.400
according to LSEG data.
That's up a million tonnes.

83
00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.400
Shipments to Asia slipped, to about
two point seven million tonnes from

84
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.640
two point eight million in September.

85
00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.840
Egypt shows how hard this
is for smaller importers.

86
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.840
QatarEnergy extended its force majeure
on the twenty-eighth of October,

87
00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.080
OilPrice dot com reports;
earlier, only a buyer had said so.

88
00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.520
With that supply gone,
Egypt's LNG bill has doubled.

89
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.680
Cairo is deferring cargoes into next
year and burning fuel oil in its

90
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.000
power plants. Its own gas output
fell to about three point six billion

91
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.133
cubic feet a day in August.

92
00:04:52.187 --> 00:04:56.640
On new supply, ADNOC Gas, part of
the Abu Dhabi National Oil Company,

93
00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.320
will supply TotalEnergies with up
to one point six million tonnes of

94
00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:05.120
LNG. The deal runs five years and
could start as early as this year.

95
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.320
And in Saudi Arabia, Aramco's profit
rose despite attacks on its assets.

96
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.480
Third-quarter adjusted net income was
thirty-one point two billion dollars,

97
00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.000
Bloomberg reported. That compares
with twenty-eight point six billion

98
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.880
a year earlier, and
beat analyst forecasts.

99
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.960
Higher prices and refining earnings
offset attacks on the East-West pipeline

100
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.320
and other facilities.

101
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.160
A separate analysis puts headline
net income at about thirty-six point

102
00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.000
three billion dollars. That's up
thirty-four point five percent.

103
00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.800
But it argues exceptional
gains lifted the figure,

104
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.360
while the physical
operations deteriorated.

105
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.560
A few more things.

106
00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.480
New Jersey Governor Mikie Sherrill
has warned port and terminal operators

107
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.680
not to accept Russian diesel
bound for the East Coast,

108
00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.000
gCaptain reported. The tanker Agioi
Fanendes is being tracked toward

109
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.493
New York and New Jersey, and
its buyer hasn't been named.

110
00:05:55.547 --> 00:05:59.120
A Western official and an Arab official
say Houthi fighters have carried

111
00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.093
out several cross-border raids
into Saudi Arabia in recent months.

112
00:06:03.147 --> 00:06:07.173
That's a claim only. Neither Riyadh
nor the Houthis have confirmed it,

113
00:06:07.227 --> 00:06:09.160
and no energy sites were named.

114
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:13.240
Shell is selling its North
West Shelf LNG stake to XRG,

115
00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.147
ADNOC's investment arm. The stake
is just under seventeen percent,

116
00:06:17.173 --> 00:06:20.800
and the price is one point four five
billion dollars plus a contingent

117
00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.680
payment.

118
00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.280
Marathon is nearing a roughly four
billion dollar sale of refineries

119
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.280
to CVR Energy, the Wall
Street Journal reported,

120
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.880
citing unnamed sources. Neither
company has confirmed it.

121
00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.360
Iraq's oil minister says terms for
West Qurna-2 are agreed with Chevron.

122
00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.760
For now, that's Baghdad's account alone.

123
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.080
And Brazil's oil output reached about
four point seven million barrels

124
00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.613
a day in September. That's up twenty
point three percent on a year earlier.

125
00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:50.720
What to watch next. Daily EU gas
storage readings run from the fifth

126
00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.373
to the tenth of November.

127
00:06:52.427 --> 00:06:56.053
The Agioi Fanendes is due in New
York and New Jersey on Saturday,

128
00:06:56.107 --> 00:06:59.920
the seventh. And on the eleventh,
the EIA's weekly report covers the

129
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.800
week to the sixth of November.

130
00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.360
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
